-- Point-in-time DATA snapshot of the catalogue tables.
-- Project: ffymjxjcnwakgdmldpne (hosted).  Captured: 2026-08-22.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS
-- One plain, read-only copy of production catalogue data, taken with
-- `supabase db dump --linked --data-only --schema public` and reduced to three
-- tables. It exists so this data survives outside the remote database. Verified
-- row counts at capture time, matching the live remote exactly:
--
--     public.court_form_library         723 rows
--     public.legal_procedure_rules       55 rows
--     public.legal_form_mapping_rules    31 rows
--
-- These tables hold reference/catalogue data, not user data. No PII.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS NOT
-- It is NOT wired into seed.sql, NOT run by `supabase db reset`, and NOT
-- automated. Nothing loads it unless a human does. It is a snapshot, not a
-- backup system, and it is stale the moment catalogue data changes on the
-- remote. It does not replace Supabase's own backups.
--
-- NOT A COMPLETE DATA BACKUP
-- Eleven other public tables also held real data at capture time and are NOT
-- included here: court_form_fields (136), court_forms (113), forms (104),
-- form_rules (50), pdf_form_inventory (50), small_claims_form_lookup (32),
-- legal_issue_rules (28), legal_question_rules (10), civil_form_lookup (8),
-- legal_evidence_rules (8), legal_risk_rules (8), legal_element_rules (7),
-- court_form_sources (6), pdf_overlay_fields (2).
--
-- RESTORING
-- The INSERTs are plain and have no ON CONFLICT clause, so they load cleanly
-- only into EMPTY tables. Against tables that already hold rows they will fail
-- on duplicate keys -- that is deliberate, so a restore cannot silently
-- half-apply. To reload intentionally, TRUNCATE the three tables first.
--
-- The trailing setval() calls restore the identity high-water marks for
-- legal_procedure_rules and legal_form_mapping_rules. Without them the next
-- INSERT into those tables would collide. court_form_library has a uuid primary
-- key and no sequence.
--
-- These tables have no foreign keys, so load order does not matter.

SET statement_timeout = 0;
SET client_encoding = 'UTF8';
SET standard_conforming_strings = on;
SELECT pg_catalog.set_config('search_path', '', false);

--
-- Data for public.court_form_library (723 rows)
--


--
-- Data for public.legal_procedure_rules (55 rows)
--


SELECT pg_catalog.setval('"public"."legal_procedure_rules_id_seq"', 55, true);

--
-- Data for public.legal_form_mapping_rules (31 rows)
--


SELECT pg_catalog.setval('"public"."legal_form_mapping_rules_id_seq"', 32, true);
